  "id": "DrugBank_DB00180 - MONDO_4765",
  "verbalization": "Flunisolide is implicated in the pathogenesis of Intrinsic Asthma through a mechanism involving the drug's indirect interaction with Ibudilast and Zileuton. The evidence suggests that Flunisolide may act as a mediator in the treatment of Asthma, with its indication for Allergic Asthma and its association with Ibudilast and Zileuton both leading to the development of Intrinsic Asthma. This implies a potential pathway where Flunisolide influences the expression or activity of Ibudilast and Zileuton, which in turn contribute to the development of Intrinsic Asthma. The overlapping pathways between Allergic Asthma and Intrinsic Asthma, as well as the shared role of Ibudilast in both, suggest a possible functional overlap in the biological processes underlying these conditions. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context when evaluating the reutilization of Flunisolide for Intrinsic Asthma.",
